          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A Kan fibration is one of the notions of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations+of+simplicial+sets"} fibrations of simplicial sets
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em Kan fibration
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon Y \to X
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial sets
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
              for all
              = succeed "-inclusions." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
          %p This means that for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Λ
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi π
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi n
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Lambda^k[n] &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow\mathrlap{{}^\pi}
                  \\\
                  \\Delta^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                  }
          %p
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\ge 1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\le k\le n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
          #eq:HornFiller.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Λ
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi π
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi n
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Lambda^k[n] &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow &amp;\nearrow&amp; \big\downarrow\mathrlap{{}^\pi}
                  \\\
                  \\Delta^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            In terms of the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powering"} powering
            of simplicial sets over sets, this is equivalent to the morphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Λ
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Y^{\Delta[n]}
                  \\to
                  Y^{\Lambda^k[n]} \times_{X^{\Lambda^k[n]}} X^{\Delta^k[n]}
          %p
            all being
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^{\Lambda^k[n]}
            is the set of tuples of
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            that glue along their boundaries to an image of the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
          %h2#illustration Illustration
          %p
            Kan fibrations are combinatorial analogs of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            of the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} model structure on topological spaces
            and the standard
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
          %p
            Recall the shape of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horns"} horns
            in low dimension.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                \-
                %strong>
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
                \- The horns
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mn 0
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^1_0
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^1_1
                of the 1-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
                are just copies of the 0-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^0
                regarded as the left and right endpoint of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n= 1
                the above condition says that for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
